From 1ae8e7a60eeef2f6c6a47061562f525338def64b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:06:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] common: accept out-of-order tool-call params in tagged
 peg-native grammar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 04/09 leniency only tolerated duplicates AFTER the required sequence;
a model emitting required parameters OUT OF SCHEMA ORDER still killed the
whole tool call (05/09 task 190228, 21:17:56Z: write emitted content then
path — turn lost, 109.7s re-prefill to resume).

The PEG star is possessive, so "each required at least once, in any order"
cannot be expressed in the grammar:

- grammar: the required-in-schema-order sequence becomes a repeat of ANY
  parameter (any order, any count; duplicates already resolve last-wins)
- required-ness moves to a post-parse completeness check in
  common_chat_peg_parse, keyed by a new arena sidecar (tool_required_args)
  that survives save/load — the server ships the parser as a string
  (optional "tool_required" JSON field; empty sidecar serializes identical
  to before, previously saved arenas stay loadable)
- a missing required param still rejects the call with the same
  "does not match the expected peg-native format" error as before, now
  with an observable marker "rejected: required param '<name>' missing"
  (parity with the strict sequence this replaces)
- unknown parameter names still fail the grammar (05/09 task 181152:
  write with <parameter=command>) — that remains a hard failure

Test: tagged_reordered_required_params (reversed order, optional before
required, reorder+duplicate last-wins, missing-required rejection with
marker, sidecar save/load roundtrip, autoparser wiring via the real Hy3
template — verified RED with the population disabled). Suites green:
test-chat-auto-parser 78/441, test-chat-peg-parser 32/198.
NOT deployed: prepared only, joint test live on optim3.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <noreply@z.ai>
